/E (Text classification for spam and phishing detection has traditionally relied on Bayesian filtering and rule-based heuristics that examine sender headers, blacklisted URLs, and known keyword patterns. Such systems are effective against previously seen campaigns but degrade quickly as attackers reword their messages or rotate infrastructure. More recent approaches apply supervised machine learning directly to message content, converting text into vector representations such as bag-of-words or TF-IDF and training discriminative classifiers such as Naive Bayes, Logistic Regression, and )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
