/P 51 0 R
/E (This paper makes three contributions. First, it presents a complete, reproducible NLP-to-ML pipeline for phishing email detection, implemented step by step and documented for educational and research use. Second, it provides a systematic comparison of four classical classifiers under identical feature- engineering conditions, together with quantitative and visual evaluation. Third, it demonstrates a practical deployment path by exporting a trained model's exact parameters and re- implementing its inference logic in JavaScript, yielding a verified, privacy-preserving, client-side prototype rather than a purely offline research artifact. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
