/P 52 0 R
/E (More recent literature has also explored deep learning and transformer-based architectures \(e.g., LSTM and BERT variants\) for phishing and spam detection, which can capture longer-range contextual dependencies than bag-of-words features at the cost of greater training data requirements and reduced interpretability. Classical linear models such as Logistic Regression, by contrast, offer directly inspectable coefficients that map individual terms to their contribution toward a prediction [8], which is a desirable property for a system intended to explain its decisions to an end user. This work builds on the classical, interpretable branch of this literature, combining established techniques into a complete, reproducible pipeline together with a lightweight, verified client-side deployment. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
