/T (C. Preprocessing Statistics After cleaning, stopwordremoval, and lemmatization, the TF- IDF vectorizer \(unigramsand bigrams, minimum document frequency of 2\) producedavocabulary of 702 terms from the 391-email corpus. Thisrelatively small, task-specific vocabulary reflects the templated nature of the working dataset; a larger, more heterogeneous real-world corpus would be expected to yield a substantially larger and more diverse vocabulary, which is one reason the results in Section VI should be interpreted as an upper bound rather than a realistic field estimate. )
/E (C. Preprocessing Statistics After cleaning, stopwordremoval, and lemmatization, the TF- IDF vectorizer \(unigramsand bigrams, minimum document frequency of 2\) producedavocabulary of 702 terms from the 391-email corpus. Thisrelatively small, task-specific vocabulary reflects the templated nature of the working dataset; a larger, more heterogeneous real-world corpus would be expected to yield a substantially larger and more diverse vocabulary, which is one reason the results in Section VI should be interpreted as an upper bound rather than a realistic field estimate. )
