/T (The system was implemented in Python 3 usingpandas and NumPy for data handling; NLTK for stopwordremoval and WordNet lemmatization [2]; scikit-learn for TF-IDF vectorization and all four classifiers [1]; matplotlib, seaborn, and WordCloud for visualization; and joblib for model persistence. Development was carried out in a Jupyter Notebook, and the trained model was additionally deployed as a client-side prototype using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, with no external runtime dependencies beyond a modern web browser. Table II summarizes the primary software components. )
/E (The system was implemented in Python 3 usingpandas and NumPy for data handling; NLTK for stopwordremoval and WordNet lemmatization [2]; scikit-learn for TF-IDF vectorization and all four classifiers [1]; matplotlib, seaborn, and WordCloud for visualization; and joblib for model persistence. Development was carried out in a Jupyter Notebook, and the trained model was additionally deployed as a client-side prototype using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, with no external runtime dependencies beyond a modern web browser. Table II summarizes the primary software components. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [13]
