/T (Beyond raw accuracy,thefourmodels differ in practical deployment characteristics.NaiveBayes trains and predicts fastest and requires theleastmemory, making it attractive for high-throughput mailservers.Logistic Regression offers the best balance of accuracyandinterpretability, as discussed above. Random Forestismorerobust to noisy or non-linear feature interactions butisslowertotrain and produces a larger, less portable model. LinearSVMoffers strong margin-based separation but requiresprobabilitycalibration, as used here, to produce the probabilityscoresneeded for a user-facing verdict. These trade-offs, ratherthanrawaccuracy alone, motivated the choice of Logistic Regressionforthe client-side prototype in Section VII. )
/E (Beyond raw accuracy,thefourmodels differ in practical deployment characteristics.NaiveBayes trains and predicts fastest and requires theleastmemory, making it attractive for high-throughput mailservers.Logistic Regression offers the best balance of accuracyandinterpretability, as discussed above. Random Forestismorerobust to noisy or non-linear feature interactions butisslowertotrain and produces a larger, less portable model. LinearSVMoffers strong margin-based separation but requiresprobabilitycalibration, as used here, to produce the probabilityscoresneeded for a user-facing verdict. These trade-offs, ratherthanrawaccuracy alone, motivated the choice of Logistic Regressionforthe client-side prototype in Section VII. )
