/T (IX. CONCLUSION  This paper presentedacomplete,workingpipelineforAI-driven phishing email detectionusingNaturalLanguageProcessing and classical MachineLearning.Thesystemsuccessfully cleans and vectorizes emailtext,trainsandcomparesmultiple classifiers, and visualizesbothmodelperformanceand word- level explainability. Thetrainedmodelwasfurtherdeployed as a live, interactive, privacy-preservingbrowserprototype, demonstrating that theapproachisoperableendtoend rather than purely theoretical.Whilecurrentresultsareinflated by the use of a small, templateddataset,thepipeline,architecture, and prototype are directlyextensibletoreal-worlddata,positioning this work as a foundationforaproduction-gradephishing detection system. Futureworkwillfocusonclosingthe gap between templated andreal-worldperformancebyretraining on larger public corporaandincorporatingsignalsbeyondmessage text, as outlined in SectionVIII.)
/E (IX. CONCLUSION  This paper presentedacomplete,workingpipelineforAI-driven phishing email detectionusingNaturalLanguageProcessing and classical MachineLearning.Thesystemsuccessfully cleans and vectorizes emailtext,trainsandcomparesmultiple classifiers, and visualizesbothmodelperformanceand word- level explainability. Thetrainedmodelwasfurtherdeployed as a live, interactive, privacy-preservingbrowserprototype, demonstrating that theapproachisoperableendtoend rather than purely theoretical.Whilecurrentresultsareinflated by the use of a small, templateddataset,thepipeline,architecture, and prototype are directlyextensibletoreal-worlddata,positioning this work as a foundationforaproduction-gradephishing detection system. Futureworkwillfocusonclosingthe gap between templated andreal-worldperformancebyretraining on larger public corporaandincorporatingsignalsbeyondmessage text, as outlined in SectionVIII.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
