385 0 obj
<<
/Title (B. Real-World Dataset Sources To scale the system beyondtheworking dataset, the following public, real-world phishingemaildatasets can be merged in by mapping their text and labelcolumns to email_text and label: the combined Enron/Ling/CEAS/Nazario/Nigerian- Fraud/SpamAssassin corpusonKaggle [3]; the Subhajournal phishing emails dataset on Kaggle[4]; the ealvaradob/phishing- dataset on Hugging Face [5];theNazario Phishing Corpus [6]; and the SpamAssassin PublicCorpus [7]. These sources vary considerably in size, rangingfrom a few thousand to over 250,000 labeled messages, andinlabel quality, so any merged corpus should be re-audited forduplicate or mislabeled entries before retraining.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 313 0 R
/Prev 355 0 R
/Next 356 0 R
>>
endobj
386 0 obj
<<
/Title (The system was implemented in Python 3 usingpandas and NumPy for data handling; NLTK for stopwordremoval and WordNet lemmatization [2]; scikit-learn for TF-IDF vectorization and all four classifiers [1]; matplotlib, seaborn, and WordCloud for visualization; and joblib for model persistence. Development was carried out in a Jupyter Notebook, and the trained model was additionally deployed as a client-side prototype using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, with no external runtime dependencies beyond a modern web browser. Table II summarizes the primary software components.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 357 0 R
/First 396 0 R
/Last 396 0 R
/Count -1
>>
endobj
