/Title (33 true negatives and 46 true positives, with zero false positives and zero false negatives. Fig. 3 presents ROC curves, each achieving an AUC of 1.00, indicating perfect separability between classes on this dataset. In practice, a false negative \(a phishing email classified as legitimate\) is the more costly error type, since it allows an attack to reach the user unflagged, while a false positive \(a legitimate email flagged as phishing\) mainly costs user convenience; the zero counts for both error types here should be read as a property of this particular templated dataset rather than a guarantee on unseen, real-world traffic.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 358 0 R
/Prev 398 0 R
/Next 406 0 R
>>
